Login in Django is full gradient background with white card split. Current Flutter login has grey background and the left panel is blue gradient (not matching). To be faithful, I should set the login background to the gradient, white card, left panel with light gradient and image, right form. The image `ingresar.png` is 20KB small. Let's update.

Select page: full gradient and header.

Register pages: full gradient, white card, left panel blue gradient.

I'll create a shared `AuthBackground` widget with gradient and decorative circles (Positioned circles), used by login, select, register. Maybe `AuthAppBar` with logo. Keep it simple.

Implementation steps:

1. `lib/presentation/widgets/auth_background.dart`:
```dart
class AuthBackground extends StatelessWidget {
  final Widget child;
  const AuthBackground({super.key, required this.child});
  build => Container(decoration: BoxDecoration(gradient: AppColors.heroGradient), child: Stack(children:[ Positioned circles, SafeArea(child: child)]))
}
```
Decorative circles: Container 500x500 white 0.1 opacity, top -200 right -100; 300 circle bottom -100 left -50.

2. `lib/presentation/widgets/auth_brand_app_bar.dart`? Could use AppBar with white bg. In Django header is white fixed; select/registro/login have it. So keep white AppBar with logo and back for these screens. Implement a helper `CuidArteAuthAppBar` extends StatelessWidget implements PreferredSizeWidget, with optional back button. Or just duplicate. Better create `auth_app_bar.dart`.

Actually the login page in Flutter already has a custom app bar with logo. Reuse. Create widget:
```dart
class CuidArteAuthAppBar extends StatelessWidget implements PreferredSizeWidget {
 final bool showBack;
 ...
 title Row logo + gradient text
}
```
Then use in all 4 screens.

3. Rewrite login screen with AuthBackground, container white radius 30, desktop Row left/right, mobile only form. Left panel light blue gradient with image + text "¡Bienvenido de nuevo!" + description using gradient text? In Django title gradient. Use ShaderMask or solid primaryDark. Use exact.

Form: labels and fields as current but "Iniciar Sesión" with gradient text maybe. Buttons gradient. Use Form validators. Submit calls auth.loginAutoDetect(email, password) returning role and route. Also show snackbar if email empty etc.

Remove any role selection. Also don't prefill credentials so no role hints. But demo testing: user might need to know credentials. Could add a subtle demo hint? Not in Django. Avoid.

4. Select account screen: use AuthBackground with exact header/cards. On mobile stacked; top accent gradient; no appbar? Django has header. Add CuidArteAuthAppBar. Cards exact. Footer with "¿Ya tienes una cuenta? Inicia sesión aquí" → pop to login. If opened from ServiciosScreen, maybe pop then? The existing behavior pop. Fine.

The select screen should not show "Cliente" role selector; it's two cards "Busco Cuidador" and "Soy Cuidador" as Django. That's exactly what image likely is.

5. Register screens: Use AuthBackground, white card. Mobile: hide left panel (Django hides on ≤968), show only form. Desktop: left panel 40%, right 60%.
Create shared `RegistrationShell` widget to reduce duplication:
```dart
class RegistrationShell extends StatelessWidget {
 final String title, subtitle;
 final Widget form;
 ...
}
```
It includes app bar and card with brand panel and scrollable form. But the form needs Form key; pass widget. Fine.

Maybe create `auth_brand_panel.dart` with `AuthValuePanel` (title, subtitle, benefits). Login uses image variant. Could just inline.

Forms:
- Use TextFormField with labels as external labels? Django labels above inputs. Flutter InputDecoration labelText floats inside. To match, use column with Text label then TextFormField with hintText. More work but better fidelity. Let's create a reusable `AuthField` widget with label, hint, controller, validator, obscure, suffix, keyboard, etc. This keeps forms clean.
- Date field: readOnly TextFormField with onTap `showDatePicker`, initialDate 1960? Must be ≥18. Validate not null. Use format dd/MM/yyyy via intl.
- Password fields with visibility toggle.
- Terms checkbox with RichText "Acepto los términos y condiciones *". Validate checkbox true.
- Specialty dropdown: DropdownButtonFormField with exact options and label "Especialidades *".
- Experience: TextFormField maxLines 3, maxLength 200, validator 5..200.
- Phone: 10 digits, maxLength 10, validator length 10.
- Names: validator min 3 letters, no numbers. Use RegExp.
- Email: validator regex.
- Password: at least one number, one uppercase, one special, length >=8.

- Submit client: call `auth.registerClientAccount(...)`; snackbar green "¡Cuenta creada! Te enviamos un correo de bienvenida a <email>."; navigate MainNavigationScreen.
- Submit caregiver: call registerCaregiverAccount; snackbar same; navigate CaregiverDashboardScreen.
- Footer link "¿Ya tienes una cuenta? Inicia sesión" pop until first? Use `Navigator.of(context).popUntil((route) => route.isFirst)` then push LoginScreen? Simpler `Navigator.of(context).pushAndRemoveUntil(MaterialPageRoute(builder: (_) => const LoginScreen()), (r) => false)` but that loses public wrapper. In Django it goes to login. Fine. However login has back button that then pops nothing. Login's back button currently `Navigator.pop`; when root, does nothing. Could use `pushReplacement` to LoginScreen.

Could use `Navigator.of(context).popUntil((route) => route.settings.name == ...)` no names. Simpler push LoginScreen.

